ros: Quick design review 1: the console's dark syntax theme + metric charts feel visually disconnected. code blocks look bright while adjacent charts are muted, which draws attention away from the data. thoughts on harmonizing without losing code readability?

mike: noticed that too. if we desaturate the chart palette slightly and introduce an accent stroke around active series, it might read as a coherent system. can you paste the current vars?

ros: pasted a trimmed set below. trying to keep base contrast for code but reduce saturation for charts: ```
--bg: #0b0d0f;
--panel: #101214;
--code-bg: #0e1317;
--code-fg: #cfeefc;
--chart-low: #3fb2a3;
--chart-mid: #ffd37b;
--chart-high: #ff6f56;
--accent: #7bd2ff;
```

tara: code fg at #cfeefc is great for syntax tokens but it's causing a halo when placed near chart legends. suggest keeping code tokens bright but adding a 1px inverse border around code blocks to help separate them. for charts: reduce saturation by ~15% and make active series outline 1.5px with --accent.

elliot: accessibility: check contrast of legend text over panel vs code block borders. small legend labels are failing 4.5:1 in some cases. also for syntax: token color differences should be >=3:1 for small text so developers can skim.

ros: new proposal: drop chart saturation, add active series stroke, add subtle separator for code blocks, and introduce an optional "Unified contrast" toggle to slightly raise chart/text contrasts across the console. updated vars snippet: ```
--chart-low: #46b6aa; /* desat */
--chart-mid: #f0c87a;
--chart-high: #ff7a66;
--code-border: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
--series-stroke: rgba(123,210,255,0.9);
```

mike: sounds good. UI copy for the toggle? maybe: "Visual coherence: Increase chart/text contrast" or shorter: "Unified contrast mode". keep tooltip: "Improves visual hierarchy between code and charts."

tara: prefer "Unified contrast" and tooltip copy: "Balances colors for charts, code, and labels to help scanning." also note: when unified contrast is on, reduce chart fill alpha for sparklines to 0.7 so code doesn't compete.

elliot: plus one. add a note to the spec: "run automated contrast checks for legend, small labels, and inline code blocks" and include examples for token-level contrast ratios.

design-bot: Uploaded Figma frame: https://figma.com/file/pqrs-syntax-chart-unify (ros/unify-contrast-pass)

ros: i'll add a Storybook control for "Unified contrast" and a test fixture showing code + chart adjacent. i'll also include the contrast checklist. will open PR and ping QA. thanks all :raised_hands:
